  "description": "It was discovered that libwebsockets did not properly validate\nuser-supplied data when parsing HTTP/2 HPACK path headers, which could\nresult in a write past the end of an allocated buffer. An attacker could\npossibly use this issue to execute arbitrary code. (CVE-2026-19773)\n\nIt was discovered that libwebsockets did not properly handle CBOR\nrecording in the LECP parser, which could result in a write past the end\nof an allocated buffer. An attacker could possibly use this issue to\ncause a crash or execute arbitrary code. (CVE-2026-78161)",
  "id": "USN-8893-1",
  "isummary": "Libwebsockets could be made to crash or run programs if it received\nspecially crafted network traffic.",
